  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.63",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p>0$, and let $\\Gamma$ be the principal congruence subgroup of $\\operatorname{Aut}(F[x_1,\\ldots,x_n])$ consisting of all automorphisms that send each variable $x_i$ to $x_i$ modulo terms of higher degree. Then $\\Gamma$ is a residually-$p$ group. Does $\\Gamma$ satisfy a pro-$p$ identity?",
